DESCRIPTION >
    - `repository_star_snapshots_by_day_ds` holds the rows of `repositoryStarSnapshots` sorted by capture day first, so a "stars as of a date" lookup reads only the days just before that date instead of each repository's full history.
    - Populated by `repository_star_snapshots_by_day_MV.pipe` on every insert into `repositoryStarSnapshots`.
    - Read by `stars_github_as_of.pipe`. Versions of one snapshot collapse on merge by `updatedAt`; readers still pick the latest with `argMax`.
    - Small granules keep a lookup for a few repositories close to their own rows: one day holds a row per repository, about 30K rows.

SCHEMA >
    `day` Date,
    `repositoryId` String,
    `capturedAt` DateTime64(3),
    `starCount` Int32,
    `updatedAt` DateTime64(3)

ENGINE ReplacingMergeTree
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY toYear(day)
ENGINE_SETTINGS index_granularity = 1024
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY day, repositoryId, capturedAt
ENGINE_VER updatedAt
